course: dictionary
lesson: 3894
title: Fret: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fret is a word with several meanings, so context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it first.
explain: The most common meaning is to worry. «Do not fret because of those who are evil» means do not worry about people who do bad things. As a noun, a fret is one of the thin metal ridges on a guitar's neck.
explain: In «Lest the awe should dwell — And turn your frolic to fret», the word frolic means play, and turn your frolic to fret shows that fret is the opposite of fun. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: To «fret» (verb) means to worry and be upset, often again and again.
fact: A «fret» (noun) is one of the thin metal ridges on a guitar's neck; you press the strings behind them to make different notes.
fact: A «sea fret» is a cold mist or fog that comes in from the sea, found in parts of the UK.
fact: The old meaning of «fret» is to rub or wear something away.
exercise: «Do not fret because of those who are evil.» What does fret mean here? | To rub something smooth | To fall asleep | *To worry and be upset | To play a tune loudly
exercise: Mia presses the strings behind the thin metal ridges on her guitar's neck. What is each ridge called? | *A fret | A chord | A sea fret | A string
exercise: «A cold grey mist rolled in from the sea and the day turned dull.» What is this mist called in parts of the UK? | A guitar fret | *A sea fret | A frolic | A fog bank of worry
test: «Lest the awe should dwell — And turn your frolic to fret.» What does fret most likely mean in this line? | Dance | Sleep | Wash | *Worry
test: Ben tends to fret over small things. What does fret over mean? | Play with | *Worry about | Forget about | Sing about
exam: Old writers used fret to say a river can fret stones smooth over time. What does fret mean here? | *To rub or wear away | To make a mist | To worry | To play music
